{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "ASV1901",
  "book_code": "PSA",
  "chapter": 109,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "PSA.109.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.109.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Hold not thy peace, O God of my praise;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.109.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.109.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For the mouth of the wicked and the mouth of deceit have they opened against me:\nThey have spoken unto me with a lying tongue.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.109.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.109.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "They have compassed me about also with words of hatred,\nAnd fought against me without a cause.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.109.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.109.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For my love they are my adversaries:\nBut I ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "give myself unto",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " prayer.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.109.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.109.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And they have rewarded me evil for good,\nAnd hatred for my love.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.109.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.109.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Set thou a wicked man over him;\nAnd let an adversary stand at his right hand.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.109.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.109.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "When he is judged, let him come forth guilty;\nAnd let his prayer be turned into sin.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.109.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.109.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Let his days be few;",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "And",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " let another take his office.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.109.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.109.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Let his children be fatherless,\nAnd his wife a widow.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.109.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.109.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Let his children be vagabonds, and beg;\nAnd let them seek ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "their bread",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " out of their desolate places.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.109.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.109.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Let the extortioner catch all that he hath;\nAnd let strangers make spoil of his labor.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.109.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.109.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Let there be none to extend kindness unto him;\nNeither let there be any to have pity on his fatherless children.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.109.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.109.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Let his posterity be cut off;\nIn the generation following let their name be blotted out.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.109.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.109.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Let the iniquity of his fathers be remembered with Jehovah;\nAnd let not the sin of his mother be blotted out.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.109.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.109.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Let them be before Jehovah continually,\nThat he may cut off the memory of them from the earth;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.109.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.109.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Because he remembered not to show kindness,\nBut persecuted the poor and needy man,\nAnd the broken in heart, to slay ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "them",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ".",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.109.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.109.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Yea, he loved cursing, and it came unto him;\nAnd he delighted not in blessing, and it was far from him.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.109.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.109.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He clothed himself also with cursing as with his garment,\nAnd it came into his inward parts like water,\nAnd like oil into his bones.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.109.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.109.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Let it be unto him as the raiment wherewith he covereth himself,\nAnd for the girdle wherewith he is girded continually.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.109.20",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.109.20",
      "verse": 20,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "This is the reward of mine adversaries from Jehovah,\nAnd of them that speak evil against my soul.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.109.21",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.109.21",
      "verse": 21,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But deal thou with me, O Jehovah the Lord, for thy name’s sake:\nBecause thy lovingkindness is good, deliver thou me;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.109.22",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.109.22",
      "verse": 22,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For I am poor and needy,\nAnd my heart is wounded within me.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.109.23",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.109.23",
      "verse": 23,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I am gone like the shadow when it declineth:\nI am tossed up and down as the locust.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.109.24",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.109.24",
      "verse": 24,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "My knees are weak through fasting;\nAnd my flesh faileth of fatness.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.109.25",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.109.25",
      "verse": 25,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I am become also a reproach unto them:\nWhen they see me, they shake their head.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.109.26",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.109.26",
      "verse": 26,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Help me, O Jehovah my God;\nOh save me according to thy lovingkindness:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.109.27",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.109.27",
      "verse": 27,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "That they may know that this is thy hand;",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "That",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " thou, Jehovah, hast done it.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.109.28",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.109.28",
      "verse": 28,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Let them curse, but bless thou:\nWhen they arise, they shall be put to shame,\nBut thy servant shall rejoice.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.109.29",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.109.29",
      "verse": 29,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Let mine adversaries be clothed with dishonor,\nAnd let them cover themselves with their own shame as with a robe.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.109.30",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.109.30",
      "verse": 30,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I will give great thanks unto Jehovah with my mouth;\nYea, I will praise him among the multitude.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.109.31",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.109.31",
      "verse": 31,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For he will stand at the right hand of the needy,\nTo save him from them that judge his soul.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    }
  ],
  "headings": [
    {
      "style": "s1",
      "text": "Vengeance invoked upon adversaries.",
      "before_verse": 1
    },
    {
      "style": "d",
      "text": "For the Chief Musician. A Psalm of David.",
      "before_verse": 1
    }
  ]
}
